1
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:43,020
It'll work out somehow.

2
00:00:55,940 --> 00:00:59,920
Anyone without a job, come to me.

3
00:00:59,920 --> 00:01:04,520
I don't have one either, so don't worry.

4
00:01:04,520 --> 00:01:11,960
Look, it's burning... Akaneru too.

5
00:01:13,420 --> 00:01:18,260
It'll work out eventually.

6
00:01:20,300 --> 00:01:23,540
You understand, right? Right, right.

7
00:01:23,540 --> 00:01:27,440
Once you understand, shut up and follow me.

8
00:01:41,960 --> 00:01:45,920
I'm Terai Yoichi, the rookie female
police officer at Kameari Park police box.

9
00:01:45,920 --> 00:01:48,620
Height: 162 cm, weight: 65 kg.

10
00:01:48,620 --> 00:01:50,160
My blood type is A.

11
00:01:50,160 --> 00:01:52,660
My life motto is the sacrifice bunt.

12
00:01:52,660 --> 00:01:54,840
You've got to work steadily at everything,
you know.

13
00:01:55,740 --> 00:01:57,000
My commute is long, but...

14
00:01:57,000 --> 00:01:59,680
a happy home with a wife and two sons.

15
00:01:59,680 --> 00:02:01,020
That was supposed to be the plan, anyway.

16
00:02:01,020 --> 00:02:03,460
Lately,
there's something I've been worried about.

17
00:02:05,800 --> 00:02:09,400
Run! Terai! A stamp rally for Dad!

18
00:02:16,180 --> 00:02:17,760
Your dream for the future?

19
00:02:18,560 --> 00:02:23,060
Our Kenji wrote an essay on the theme of
"dreams for the future."

20
00:02:23,500 --> 00:02:25,380
What kind of dream did he write about?

21
00:02:25,940 --> 00:02:27,500
Like being a pro baseball player,

22
00:02:27,940 --> 00:02:28,940
or a doctor.

23
00:02:29,900 --> 00:02:32,320
But what he wrote was a steady, modest life.

24
00:02:32,320 --> 00:02:36,320
One day,
when I was looking over my kid's essay,

25
00:02:36,880 --> 00:02:42,080
he wrote about getting a fixed salary every month,
saving money, and building a small house.

26
00:02:43,120 --> 00:02:48,100
He wrote that he wants a stable, modest
life all the way to old age, didn't he?

27
00:02:48,960 --> 00:02:50,260
That's admirable, isn't it?

28
00:02:51,100 --> 00:02:53,180
Steady and realistic,

29
00:02:54,520 --> 00:02:58,740
but that being the future dream
of a nine-year-old son is...

30
00:03:01,240 --> 00:03:02,460
a bit sad, isn't it.

31
00:03:03,680 --> 00:03:08,200
Personally, I think a down-to-earth
life like that suits me best.

32
00:03:08,200 --> 00:03:10,560
But when we were kids,
we wanted something more...

33
00:03:11,260 --> 00:03:11,980
I understand.

34
00:03:11,980 --> 00:03:16,300
I think children's dreams
can be wildly ambitious,

35
00:03:17,840 --> 00:03:19,880
like becoming an astronaut, for example.

36
00:03:20,280 --> 00:03:21,700
Like father, like son.

37
00:03:21,700 --> 00:03:26,200
A brat who sees Terai's stingy
way of living up close every day

38
00:03:26,200 --> 00:03:28,620
can't possibly have lofty dreams.

39
00:03:31,940 --> 00:03:33,060
Ryo-san

40
00:03:34,400 --> 00:03:37,020
In the Terai household,
where life is all sacrifice bunts,

41
00:03:37,020 --> 00:03:40,380
a child grows up with the
same sacrifice-bunt outlook.

42
00:03:40,380 --> 00:03:42,800
That's just the natural order of things.

43
00:03:43,360 --> 00:03:46,620
Naturally, if I, who swing for
the fences in life, had a family,

44
00:03:46,620 --> 00:03:49,280
my child would grow up
swinging for the fences too.

45
00:03:52,100 --> 00:03:54,860
Yay, Daddy! Another home run!

46
00:03:56,920 --> 00:03:58,444
Still, no matter what anyone says,

47
00:03:58,494 --> 00:04:01,500
kids always hope their
dad will hit a big one.

48
00:04:02,080 --> 00:04:03,100
Do you really think so?

49
00:04:03,100 --> 00:04:05,940
Home runs have nothing to do with me,
after all.

50
00:04:06,860 --> 00:04:08,440
There's Ichiro, isn't there?

51
00:04:08,980 --> 00:04:11,480
Ichiro? The Ichiro from the major leagues?

52
00:04:11,940 --> 00:04:12,300
Yeah.

53
00:04:14,280 --> 00:04:15,628
Even with a sacrifice bunt,

54
00:04:15,678 --> 00:04:19,511
if you run past first base faster than the ball,
like Ichiro does,

55
00:04:19,561 --> 00:04:20,960
it's a proper infield hit.

56
00:04:21,700 --> 00:04:23,620
We won't lose to the home-run hitters.

57
00:04:23,620 --> 00:04:26,100
My kids are big Ichiro fans.

58
00:04:27,340 --> 00:04:30,960
Right, even if home runs are impossible,
maybe with an infield hit...

59
00:04:32,320 --> 00:04:34,360
I might be able to hit like that too.

60
00:04:41,140 --> 00:04:44,280
If I keep working hard with
a bunt-single approach to life,

61
00:04:44,280 --> 00:04:47,640
the kids might be able to
dream about the future too.

62
00:04:48,780 --> 00:04:50,060
Thanks, Nakagawa.

63
00:04:51,700 --> 00:04:56,000
Well, when all is said and done, it's the home run!
Hit one big bomb and you're number one, right?

64
00:04:56,000 --> 00:05:00,920
Hey, did you know there's an Ichiro
stamp rally this coming Sunday?

65
00:05:03,040 --> 00:05:09,040
A stamp rally visiting places connected to Ichiro,
the major leaguer Kameari produced.

66
00:05:09,040 --> 00:05:13,620
First prize is an Ichiro-signed bat. Hmm.

67
00:05:14,380 --> 00:05:19,520
Wow, what a coincidence!
I'm going to join this stamp rally,

68
00:05:19,520 --> 00:05:25,360
and do my best for the kids. That's the spirit,
Terai, living life by the bunt-single approach.

69
00:05:25,360 --> 00:05:31,080
Get me Ichiro's bat, okay?
Yeah, Ichiro's bat is mine.

70
00:05:31,600 --> 00:05:36,100
Eeeeeh! Aren't you only interested
in home-run hitters, senpai?

71
00:05:36,600 --> 00:05:43,600
For an Ichiro-signed bat, there must be tens of thousands
of people willing to pay any amount of money for it.

72
00:05:44,120 --> 00:05:46,480
A once-in-a-lifetime
chance to strike it rich!

73
00:05:50,140 --> 00:05:56,300
We now begin the Ichiro Stamp Rally,
honoring the major leaguer Kameari produced!

74
00:05:57,000 --> 00:06:03,240
Visit the places linked to Ichiro, collect every
stamp in your stamp book, and reach the goal.

75
00:06:03,240 --> 00:06:05,280
There sure are a lot of people.

76
00:06:05,680 --> 00:06:06,040
Yeah.

77
00:06:06,040 --> 00:06:07,240
This is insane.

78
00:06:07,240 --> 00:06:08,700
Senpai.

79
00:06:08,700 --> 00:06:13,020
We have to get out of this crowd as fast as we can,
or it's hopeless.

80
00:06:13,020 --> 00:06:14,680
You'll end up on the injured list!

81
00:06:14,680 --> 00:06:17,860
So a fast start is the deciding factor?

82
00:06:19,520 --> 00:06:22,640
Well, either way,
I'm the one who's taking that bat.

83
00:06:22,640 --> 00:06:24,840
I'm not giving it to you, Ryo-san.

84
00:06:24,840 --> 00:06:26,460
Alright, nice fight!

85
00:06:26,860 --> 00:06:30,420
You need that kind of spirit to get Ichiro's bat,
after all.

86
00:06:30,420 --> 00:06:31,540
Well then, I'll go ahead...

87
00:06:32,500 --> 00:06:33,480
S-senpai!

88
00:06:35,340 --> 00:06:35,880
Whoa!

89
00:06:37,060 --> 00:06:39,660
Damn, there's still that many
people ahead of us to the front!

90
00:06:40,680 --> 00:06:42,880
As usual, what incredible stamina.

91
00:06:42,880 --> 00:06:44,780
Terai-san, Kei-chan!

92
00:06:45,500 --> 00:06:47,220
Daddy!

93
00:06:48,300 --> 00:06:50,420
Those are Terai-san's kids.

94
00:06:50,420 --> 00:06:52,760
Sure enough, it's Kenji and Koji.

95
00:06:53,420 --> 00:06:54,920
Good luck, go for it!

96
00:06:56,640 --> 00:06:58,660
Makoto, look, over there!

97
00:06:59,200 --> 00:07:00,140
Daddy.

98
00:07:00,600 --> 00:07:01,140
Makoto.

99
00:07:01,900 --> 00:07:03,640
Alright, alright, just take it out already.

100
00:07:04,660 --> 00:07:06,460
Hey, what the hell are you doing?

101
00:07:06,460 --> 00:07:07,760
Sorry.

102
00:07:19,600 --> 00:07:20,580
Damn it!

103
00:07:22,020 --> 00:07:25,380
Ryo-chan, Terai and the
others have already gone ahead!

104
00:07:25,380 --> 00:07:27,400
Shut up! Shut up! Shut up!

105
00:07:28,020 --> 00:07:30,460
That bastard! I'll never forgive him!

106
00:07:31,520 --> 00:07:33,560
Ryo-san, you're amazing!

107
00:07:43,140 --> 00:07:43,580
Are you okay?

108
00:07:44,280 --> 00:07:44,720
Are you okay?

109
00:07:44,720 --> 00:07:49,240
Eeeeeh! Okay, the stamp rally is this way!

110
00:07:51,100 --> 00:07:55,580
Right, first we pray at the shrine.
Damn, at a time this busy!

111
00:07:57,300 --> 00:08:02,980
Come on, we're at the grounds, get those stamps!
Do they still charge money for the offering box?

112
00:08:04,240 --> 00:08:05,360
Can't be helped.

113
00:08:07,680 --> 00:08:09,760
Please, let me win first place.

114
00:08:09,760 --> 00:08:14,640
Okay, I've started the playback,
hurry up and get the stamp!

115
00:08:14,640 --> 00:08:19,960
Now, let me tell you about this
shrine's connection to Ichiro.

116
00:08:19,960 --> 00:08:24,280
I can't sit here and listen to this!
Whoa, alright!

117
00:08:24,280 --> 00:08:32,420
Honestly, kids these days... Now, as for you,
the connection between this shrine and Ichiro

118
00:08:32,420 --> 00:08:34,880
let me tell you about in detail. Haa.

119
00:08:36,020 --> 00:08:38,980
To begin with, the first meeting
between this shrine and Ichiro

120
00:08:39,460 --> 00:08:41,700
was when Ichiro was in the
second grade of elementary school.

121
00:08:42,180 --> 00:08:44,800
dashing up that famous steep staircase

122
00:08:44,800 --> 00:08:48,700
and praying in this main hall for his
dream of playing in the Major Leagues.

123
00:09:01,900 --> 00:09:02,620
Surprised!

124
00:09:02,620 --> 00:09:03,620
Terai-san!

125
00:09:04,880 --> 00:09:06,300
Everyone's already gone ahead, you know!

126
00:09:06,300 --> 00:09:07,640
Nakagawa-kun.

127
00:09:07,640 --> 00:09:09,120
Come on, hurry up!

128
00:09:10,300 --> 00:09:11,360
Wait up!

129
00:09:11,840 --> 00:09:12,640
Let's go!

130
00:09:12,860 --> 00:09:13,760
Terai!

131
00:09:14,360 --> 00:09:15,180
Push!

132
00:09:15,560 --> 00:09:16,140
Right!

133
00:09:19,340 --> 00:09:22,220
What are you doing? Hurry up!

134
00:09:24,540 --> 00:09:26,420
Come on, let's go.

135
00:09:29,580 --> 00:09:32,580
Now, for the rematch!

136
00:09:32,580 --> 00:09:32,940
Woah!

137
00:09:33,600 --> 00:09:34,440
Whoa!

138
00:09:41,980 --> 00:09:43,520
This shrine and

139
00:09:44,080 --> 00:09:44,960
Ichiro

140
00:09:45,340 --> 00:09:46,200
the player

141
00:09:52,820 --> 00:09:53,600
Here!

142
00:09:53,600 --> 00:09:54,800
Well?

143
00:09:54,800 --> 00:09:55,840
Damn it!

144
00:09:55,840 --> 00:09:56,800
Another miss?

145
00:09:57,320 --> 00:09:58,260
Hey, please!

146
00:09:58,260 --> 00:09:59,120
Just stamp it for me!

147
00:09:59,120 --> 00:10:00,300
If you win, sure.

148
00:10:00,300 --> 00:10:01,000
Damn it!

149
00:10:02,760 --> 00:10:03,700
One entry's worth.

150
00:10:03,700 --> 00:10:04,620
Here you go.

151
00:10:04,620 --> 00:10:06,900
Damn it, back of the line again?

152
00:10:10,400 --> 00:10:13,060
No, you can't! Get in line properly!

153
00:10:13,060 --> 00:10:13,840
What's your problem?

154
00:10:13,840 --> 00:10:15,580
What was that?

155
00:10:15,580 --> 00:10:18,900
So it was you at the start? You've got some nerve,
messing with me like that!

156
00:10:18,900 --> 00:10:21,500
You're the one who bumped into me first.

157
00:10:21,500 --> 00:10:23,240
Well, congratulations!

158
00:10:23,240 --> 00:10:24,840
You're both winners!

159
00:10:24,840 --> 00:10:25,700
What?

160
00:10:25,700 --> 00:10:26,640
Yes!

161
00:10:26,640 --> 00:10:28,000
Here you go.

162
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:29,100
Let's go.

163
00:10:29,100 --> 00:10:30,580
Damn it.

164
00:10:32,580 --> 00:10:39,540
Any lucky ones? Miss, thanks for your trouble, next in line.
Another miss, yeah, yeah, good work.

165
00:10:40,640 --> 00:10:46,740
Alright, finally my turn. First prize?
Got it, that's for ten draws.

166
00:10:47,240 --> 00:10:53,180
Aaah, hold on, what's this?
There are only two winning numbers!

167
00:10:54,560 --> 00:10:55,700
What are you doing?

168
00:10:56,320 --> 00:10:59,500
Look at this! The rest are all misses!

169
00:10:59,500 --> 00:11:03,240
Hurry up and bring out a new box!

170
00:11:03,240 --> 00:11:04,820
Got it.

171
00:11:05,660 --> 00:11:06,380
Here you go.

172
00:11:06,380 --> 00:11:09,320
Alright, ten draws! I'm going all in!

173
00:11:11,320 --> 00:11:11,740
Go, go, go!

174
00:11:12,200 --> 00:11:13,620
Haa, haa, haa.

175
00:11:13,620 --> 00:11:15,000
So, how about that?

176
00:11:16,100 --> 00:11:17,380
They're all misses!

177
00:11:18,240 --> 00:11:19,300
No way!

178
00:11:19,800 --> 00:11:21,020
Yeah, yeah, good work.

179
00:11:21,020 --> 00:11:24,800
You disrupted business,
so you go back to the end of the line. Next!

180
00:11:24,800 --> 00:11:25,600
What?!

181
00:11:26,160 --> 00:11:27,380
Back to the end of the line again?

182
00:11:28,020 --> 00:11:29,600
Ryo-san.

183
00:11:29,600 --> 00:11:31,020
It's you two.

184
00:11:31,020 --> 00:11:32,920
Coming now won't get you a winning draw.

185
00:11:33,940 --> 00:11:35,760
Yeah, anyway, I'll do my best.

186
00:11:36,340 --> 00:11:37,380
Miss.

187
00:11:37,820 --> 00:11:38,680
Alright, next!

188
00:11:39,220 --> 00:11:40,340
Two portions, please.

189
00:11:43,180 --> 00:11:44,560
I won!

190
00:11:44,560 --> 00:11:45,380
What?

191
00:11:45,380 --> 00:11:47,760
Terai, we did it!

192
00:11:47,760 --> 00:11:50,820
I can't believe winning is this easy.

193
00:11:50,820 --> 00:11:52,420
Ring the bell!

194
00:11:52,420 --> 00:11:53,360
R-right.

195
00:11:54,200 --> 00:11:56,180
Terai, go on ahead.

196
00:11:56,720 --> 00:11:57,020
Yeah.

197
00:11:57,020 --> 00:11:59,600
I didn't win anything either.

198
00:11:59,600 --> 00:11:59,840
What?

199
00:11:59,840 --> 00:12:02,620
Why only you two?

200
00:12:03,520 --> 00:12:04,900
I'll take you down.

201
00:12:04,900 --> 00:12:05,580
Yes.

202
00:12:08,500 --> 00:12:09,860
Sorry, kid.

203
00:12:11,320 --> 00:12:13,880
You're still young,
you'll have plenty of chances!

204
00:12:14,440 --> 00:12:17,440
Here's the money for ten draws!
Try again with this!

205
00:12:17,620 --> 00:12:18,140
See ya!

206
00:12:18,920 --> 00:12:19,960
Hey, you!

207
00:12:20,380 --> 00:12:23,900
Damn it, you cheated!

208
00:12:38,500 --> 00:12:41,100
There it is! That's the next checkpoint!

209
00:12:43,120 --> 00:12:43,480
Hello!

210
00:12:43,980 --> 00:12:46,920
Terai, are you also
doing Ichiro's stamp rally?

211
00:12:47,120 --> 00:12:49,840
I'll stamp it once you've
finished your ramen, okay?

212
00:12:49,840 --> 00:12:50,660
Okay!

213
00:12:50,660 --> 00:12:53,160
Hey! Hurry up!

214
00:12:54,420 --> 00:12:55,700
No need to rush, no need to rush.

215
00:12:55,700 --> 00:12:58,540
Ichiro's a big fan of our chashu noodles,
you know.

216
00:12:58,900 --> 00:13:01,160
Even now,
he comes to eat them on his trips home.

217
00:13:01,640 --> 00:13:04,020
Excuse me, is this Ichiro's stamp rally?

218
00:13:05,340 --> 00:13:07,260
Well, my brat is...

219
00:13:07,920 --> 00:13:09,360
Mine too.

220
00:13:09,360 --> 00:13:10,700
Let's do our best, shall we?

221
00:13:11,340 --> 00:13:13,460
There's only one autographed bat, right?

222
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:16,080
So we're rivals

223
00:13:16,620 --> 00:13:17,340
Here, Yūmoji.

224
00:13:18,200 --> 00:13:19,000
Alright, here we go!

225
00:13:19,000 --> 00:13:20,160
Here you go, Terai-san.

226
00:13:20,160 --> 00:13:21,600
Two at once

227
00:13:22,320 --> 00:13:23,420
Sorry.

228
00:13:24,320 --> 00:13:25,540
Alright, let's go.

229
00:13:28,900 --> 00:13:33,100
Well, I started with the broth,
so I'll have some too. Thanks.

230
00:13:45,280 --> 00:13:47,940
Come on, apologize.

231
00:13:49,960 --> 00:13:53,660
Hey, how come you're eating ramen first?

232
00:13:53,660 --> 00:13:55,860
You haven't even drawn a winning lot,
have you?

233
00:13:55,860 --> 00:13:56,620
Shut up and get out of the way!

234
00:13:56,620 --> 00:13:57,520
Hey!

235
00:13:57,920 --> 00:13:59,700
What a piece of work.

236
00:14:06,300 --> 00:14:07,200
Somebody help!

237
00:14:13,360 --> 00:14:14,320
Hey, are you okay?

238
00:14:16,700 --> 00:14:17,580
Uh-oh.

239
00:14:18,860 --> 00:14:21,440
Sorry, but I'm leaving.

240
00:14:24,620 --> 00:14:28,200
Actually, going around that way is
shorter than cutting through the park.

241
00:14:28,700 --> 00:14:29,100
Thanks.

242
00:14:36,420 --> 00:14:37,220
Let go!

243
00:14:37,220 --> 00:14:37,720
No way.

244
00:14:37,720 --> 00:14:39,980
Hachirō's bat is mine.

245
00:14:39,980 --> 00:14:43,080
What you really want isn't the bat,
it's the money, senpai.

246
00:14:43,080 --> 00:14:44,420
It's all the same.

247
00:14:44,420 --> 00:14:46,680
It's completely different.

248
00:14:46,680 --> 00:14:50,120
Why are you so partial to Terai, Nakagawa?

249
00:14:50,600 --> 00:14:54,060
I just want Terai-san to win first prize.

250
00:14:54,060 --> 00:14:54,600
Right, Sakagawa-kun!

251
00:14:56,200 --> 00:14:57,940
Hey, you two, help out!

252
00:15:00,440 --> 00:15:01,240
Terai-san!

253
00:15:02,940 --> 00:15:04,760
Apparently the baby's about to be born.

254
00:15:04,760 --> 00:15:05,600
What?

255
00:15:06,220 --> 00:15:09,060
Hey, the hospital's right there.
Can you walk?

256
00:15:10,240 --> 00:15:12,560
No good, I can't walk.

257
00:15:13,140 --> 00:15:16,620
Can't Fine, let's all carry him.

258
00:15:20,200 --> 00:15:22,280
Senpai, are you okay?

259
00:15:22,280 --> 00:15:23,940
It's nothing!

260
00:15:23,940 --> 00:15:27,060
Never mind that, keep an eye on
him so he doesn't fall off the bench.

261
00:15:28,800 --> 00:15:30,120
Hang in there.

262
00:15:30,120 --> 00:15:32,100
All right, we're here.

263
00:15:33,380 --> 00:15:34,820
Everything's going to be fine now.

264
00:15:35,320 --> 00:15:36,900
Don't worry, okay?

265
00:15:36,900 --> 00:15:38,680
Phew, thank goodness.

266
00:15:39,220 --> 00:15:40,300
Hey, Senpai.

267
00:15:44,080 --> 00:15:44,960
I see.

268
00:15:44,960 --> 00:15:47,620
This is the hospital where
Hachiro was born, right?

269
00:15:48,180 --> 00:15:48,860
Terai-san.

270
00:15:51,740 --> 00:15:53,240
Terai-san?

271
00:15:54,700 --> 00:15:56,320
Keep going! Keep going!

272
00:15:56,580 --> 00:15:58,000
Breathe in, breathe in, and breathe out!

273
00:15:58,180 --> 00:16:01,360
Hee-hee-hoo! Hee-hee-hoo!

274
00:16:12,720 --> 00:16:15,340
That's fast! What speed is this?

275
00:16:15,740 --> 00:16:17,000
It's 150 km.

276
00:16:17,480 --> 00:16:22,340
I heard Ichiro practiced against even
faster pitches since junior high school.

277
00:16:23,100 --> 00:16:23,980
150 km?

278
00:16:26,140 --> 00:16:28,120
Like I could hit five pitches this fast!

279
00:16:28,120 --> 00:16:29,960
At least make it three.

280
00:16:30,340 --> 00:16:31,120
Understood.

281
00:16:31,480 --> 00:16:33,040
Then three pitches will do.

282
00:16:33,400 --> 00:16:37,080
But you'll have to keep buying
pitches until you hit three.

283
00:16:37,080 --> 00:16:38,060
Damn it.

284
00:16:38,600 --> 00:16:40,300
They take 100 yen for just three pitches!

285
00:16:40,300 --> 00:16:43,040
If you don't hit them quickly,
who knows how much this will cost you!

286
00:16:47,360 --> 00:16:49,500
Even you can't lay a finger on it

287
00:16:50,380 --> 00:16:51,540
It's you again.

288
00:16:51,540 --> 00:16:53,720
Your streak of good luck ends here,
you scoundrel.

289
00:16:54,920 --> 00:16:55,880
Alright, bring it on.

290
00:16:57,540 --> 00:16:59,780
Now then, let's see what you've got.

291
00:17:00,540 --> 00:17:04,320
What good is it if you can't
hit 150 or 160 km/h pitches?

292
00:17:04,320 --> 00:17:06,720
I wonder how long that confidence will last.

293
00:17:07,120 --> 00:17:08,140
Just watch.

294
00:17:12,240 --> 00:17:13,200
Fast!

295
00:17:13,200 --> 00:17:15,400
I doubt you even grazed it.

296
00:17:15,400 --> 00:17:17,380
Well, that one was just practice.

297
00:17:17,380 --> 00:17:19,600
Alright, time to get serious.

298
00:17:19,600 --> 00:17:21,960
Damn it!

299
00:17:25,320 --> 00:17:27,520
The senior officers are still here.

300
00:17:27,520 --> 00:17:29,660
Yeah, they might catch up with us.

301
00:17:35,500 --> 00:17:37,680
There's no way I can hit that!

302
00:17:38,320 --> 00:17:40,020
Alright, I'll bunt!

303
00:17:41,980 --> 00:17:45,120
Alright, this time for sure!

304
00:17:49,720 --> 00:17:52,400
I won't lose! Bring it on!

305
00:17:53,680 --> 00:17:59,000
Whoa! Whoa, whoa! Yes! I hit it!

306
00:18:00,100 --> 00:18:03,490
Number six, just two more pitches left!
That's amazing, isn't it,

307
00:18:03,540 --> 00:18:04,360
Terai-san!

308
00:18:05,440 --> 00:18:06,840
It's a bunt, after all.

309
00:18:07,180 --> 00:18:09,540
Hitting even a bunt is amazing.

310
00:18:09,540 --> 00:18:11,240
If it's a bunt,

311
00:18:14,460 --> 00:18:15,700
Hit again!

312
00:18:17,060 --> 00:18:18,380
Just one more pitch.

313
00:18:19,260 --> 00:18:19,880
Yes!

314
00:18:19,880 --> 00:18:21,740
I hit it!

315
00:18:23,260 --> 00:18:25,440
Two more for the first and second batters.

316
00:18:30,440 --> 00:18:31,400
Yes!

317
00:18:31,400 --> 00:18:34,460
Aaaah! Three more, then nine!

318
00:18:35,220 --> 00:18:40,740
Everyone's swinging at the batting center like it's nothing, bam bam!
It's all because they read about it, honestly.

319
00:18:41,360 --> 00:18:49,920
This is no time for that! I hit it too...
What are you doing, senior, even you?

320
00:18:50,460 --> 00:18:55,180
Whatever, I'll get Ichiro's autographed bat.
Needs must.

321
00:18:56,900 --> 00:19:00,000
Yes! All three pitches hit!

322
00:19:00,480 --> 00:19:01,100
Yes.

323
00:19:01,100 --> 00:19:02,180
Thanks.

324
00:19:03,100 --> 00:19:04,760
Come again!

325
00:19:09,980 --> 00:19:10,580
Right?

326
00:19:20,980 --> 00:19:22,620
Right, step right up!

327
00:19:22,620 --> 00:19:25,220
What now?

328
00:19:25,220 --> 00:19:27,020
Thirty pitches.

329
00:19:27,020 --> 00:19:28,740
I win, since I picked
it up first and kept it.

330
00:19:28,740 --> 00:19:29,440
Here I go!

331
00:19:29,440 --> 00:19:32,320
Alright, here goes!

332
00:19:35,280 --> 00:19:36,340
One pitch.

333
00:19:36,340 --> 00:19:38,980
One pitch.

334
00:19:41,260 --> 00:19:42,480
Ten pitches.

335
00:19:42,480 --> 00:19:43,920
Thirty-three pitches.

336
00:19:43,920 --> 00:19:45,840
Twenty pitches.

337
00:19:45,840 --> 00:19:47,760
Twenty-four pitches.

338
00:19:47,760 --> 00:19:49,680
Twenty-six pitches.

339
00:19:52,240 --> 00:19:54,080
28 pitches

340
00:19:54,080 --> 00:19:56,340
28 pitches

341
00:19:56,340 --> 00:19:59,440
29 pitches

342
00:19:59,440 --> 00:20:01,080
29 pitches

343
00:20:01,080 --> 00:20:03,080
30 pitches

344
00:20:03,080 --> 00:20:05,520
Alright, the stamp!

345
00:20:06,080 --> 00:20:08,860
30 pitches

346
00:20:18,300 --> 00:20:21,380
Come on, if we get through this alley,
the goal is right there.

347
00:20:22,740 --> 00:20:25,020
Yes, yes, we got first prize!

348
00:20:32,920 --> 00:20:33,940
The notebook's

349
00:20:35,700 --> 00:20:36,540
Notebook

350
00:20:37,800 --> 00:20:39,840
Bachua hit it!

351
00:20:55,560 --> 00:20:58,360
God is watching when you do bad things,
you know.

352
00:21:00,360 --> 00:21:02,540
I was determined to win first prize,
you see.

353
00:21:03,420 --> 00:21:07,640
Even a useless old dad like me
wants to show my son a dream.

354
00:21:11,780 --> 00:21:14,580
If I keep working hard with my
infield-hit approach to life,

355
00:21:14,580 --> 00:21:17,620
maybe the kids can have
dreams for the future too.

356
00:21:19,020 --> 00:21:21,300
Hurry up, hurry up, go!

357
00:21:22,540 --> 00:21:24,140
The others are catching up!

358
00:21:24,820 --> 00:21:28,140
You've got a kid you want to
show a dream to too, right?

359
00:21:31,620 --> 00:21:31,980
Here.

360
00:21:35,340 --> 00:21:36,220
Here, take this.

361
00:21:37,640 --> 00:21:39,340
What are you talking about, mister?

362
00:21:39,980 --> 00:21:40,640
Terai-san!

363
00:21:41,940 --> 00:21:43,380
Let go, Nakagawa!

364
00:21:43,900 --> 00:21:46,040
Terai-san, please hurry!

365
00:21:46,460 --> 00:21:48,760
Come on, he said to hurry, so hurry up!

366
00:21:48,760 --> 00:21:50,480
That's for you...

367
00:21:51,120 --> 00:21:53,120
Never mind that, run!

368
00:21:56,140 --> 00:21:58,640
You're going to show your son a dream,
aren't you?

369
00:22:00,500 --> 00:22:03,320
Yeah... sorry.

370
00:22:07,140 --> 00:22:07,880
Haa...

371
00:22:08,740 --> 00:22:10,880
Tearfully...

372
00:22:12,420 --> 00:22:13,960
Congratulations!

373
00:22:14,560 --> 00:22:18,400
It's the first-prize sword,
signed by Hachirō!

374
00:22:19,560 --> 00:22:23,520
After all that effort,
we only get a keychain for participating?

375
00:22:23,520 --> 00:22:27,580
Haha, Daddy didn't even get
a participation prize. Sorry.

376
00:22:28,200 --> 00:22:29,460
It's fine, really.

377
00:22:29,460 --> 00:22:32,320
Well, dear, shall we head home soon?

378
00:22:34,080 --> 00:22:36,520
Excuse me, wait a second!

379
00:22:37,060 --> 00:22:38,820
Mister first-prize winner!

380
00:22:39,560 --> 00:22:41,240
My son, Makoto.

381
00:22:41,240 --> 00:22:42,080
Hello.

382
00:22:42,840 --> 00:22:45,700
Hello, these are our Kenji and Kōji.

383
00:22:46,180 --> 00:22:46,660
Hello.

384
00:22:47,280 --> 00:22:47,760
Hello.

385
00:22:47,760 --> 00:22:48,680
Hello.

386
00:22:50,980 --> 00:22:52,000
Can we touch it?

387
00:22:52,000 --> 00:22:52,760
Yeah.

388
00:22:53,680 --> 00:22:56,780
Wow, that's amazing! It really is signed!

389
00:22:56,780 --> 00:22:57,900
Of course it is.

390
00:23:01,380 --> 00:23:03,320
Is it "thank you" or "I'm sorry"?

391
00:23:03,800 --> 00:23:05,280
What am I supposed to say, anyway?

392
00:23:06,320 --> 00:23:09,460
That's great, really, it's great.

393
00:23:09,920 --> 00:23:12,580
Terai-san said she dropped her notebook, but

394
00:23:12,580 --> 00:23:15,100
could it be that she gave her
own notebook to that person?

395
00:23:15,100 --> 00:23:17,520
You only realized that now?

396
00:23:18,080 --> 00:23:20,280
See, that's exactly what I said.

397
00:23:20,280 --> 00:23:23,100
In the end, Terai just keeps
quietly laying down sacrifice bunts,

398
00:23:23,100 --> 00:23:25,660
she's simply suited to helping others along.

399
00:23:25,660 --> 00:23:28,100
Her whole life is one big sacrifice bunt,
that's what they say.

400
00:23:29,100 --> 00:23:29,800
Terai-san

401
00:23:30,520 --> 00:23:33,000
By the way, you betrayed me

402
00:23:33,000 --> 00:23:36,100
but I still haven't heard
why you took Terai's side.

403
00:23:37,660 --> 00:23:39,620
My father, so to speak,

404
00:23:39,620 --> 00:23:42,060
is a superhuman home-run slugger type.

405
00:23:42,640 --> 00:23:43,040
So,

406
00:23:43,040 --> 00:23:45,200
children don't necessarily

407
00:23:45,200 --> 00:23:47,660
want their fathers to hit home runs,

408
00:23:47,660 --> 00:23:49,220
I suppose that's what I wanted to say.

409
00:23:49,220 --> 00:23:50,660
Yeah, that's all.

410
00:23:50,660 --> 00:23:51,300
Yes.

411
00:23:52,220 --> 00:23:53,860
Then say it with your mouth,
not your actions.

412
00:24:19,980 --> 00:24:27,480
Probably don't want to become
someone who gambles everything on looks

413
00:24:27,480 --> 00:24:34,420
When I'm dawdling at the corner,
the moon slips away

414
00:24:34,420 --> 00:24:42,640
Now isn't everything,
so don't get too worked up

415
00:24:42,640 --> 00:24:46,380
Even if you cheat a little with lies

416
00:24:46,380 --> 00:24:50,540
Sometimes while helping someone

417
00:24:50,540 --> 00:24:53,550
Baby, do you know me?

418
00:24:53,600 --> 00:24:54,620
Toward tomorrow

419
00:24:54,620 --> 00:24:56,740
Nice spirit

420
00:24:58,100 --> 00:25:01,900
Don't rot away, I'll do what needs doing

421
00:25:01,900 --> 00:25:04,320
Cute spirit

422
00:25:04,320 --> 00:25:07,740
What's hard to tell is

423
00:25:08,900 --> 00:25:11,200
they want it to look that way.

424
00:25:13,420 --> 00:25:17,320
Isn't that better than a makeover?

425
00:25:19,460 --> 00:25:23,660
Na-na-na-na-na-na-na-na-na-na-na

426
00:25:30,100 --> 00:25:32,160
Robot Police Officer 0045

427
00:25:32,160 --> 00:25:35,500
Are you really made with
cutting-edge technology?

428
00:25:35,500 --> 00:25:37,940
Everything you're made to do, you screw up!

429
00:25:38,420 --> 00:25:40,620
Alright, I'll give you a name.

430
00:25:40,620 --> 00:25:43,580
Your name's Dame-Tarō,
you're a total failure.

431
00:25:43,580 --> 00:25:47,240
Next time: Robot Officer Dame-Tarō,
stay tuned!

432
00:25:52,740 --> 00:25:53,140
Thank you.

